  "editable": true,
  "description": "TP-Link Kasa / Tapo smart plugs exported by KasaMonitor: power, voltage, current, energy, cost, online/offline and relay per plug.",
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**KasaMonitor** — TP-Link Kasa (legacy) and Tapo (KLAP / AES) plugs with energy metering: power (W), voltage (V), current (A), energy (kWh) and cost per plug. KasaMonitor polls the plugs every 10 s and exposes `/metrics`; Prometheus scrapes it (job `kasa`). `kasa_power_total` is **cumulative Wh**; kWh = Wh / 1000. Energy over a range = sum of the counter's 5-minute increases (a drop, e.g. after a restart or a plug reset, is not counted; a scrape gap longer than 5 minutes loses the energy of that gap). Cost = kWh × **$tariff $currency/kWh** (dashboard variables, top left). 30-day windows are complete only after 30 days of data. A plug that is unplugged or off Wi-Fi shows **offline** (red); W/V/A/relay keep the last good reading. A plug withdrawn in KasaMonitor (/plugs, \"Retrage\") is no longer polled and disappears from the metrics. Voltage and current appear only for plugs that report them."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Power now",
      "description": "Sum of instantaneous power (W) of all plugs: sum(sum by (alias) (kasa_power_load)).",
