    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Plugs",
      "description": "One row per plug. online = answered the last poll; relay = on/off (last good reading). W/V/A = last reading; kWh / cost = sum of the counter's 5-minute increases in the window. Last online: within 30 days, 5-minute resolution (empty = not online in 30 days). model / protocol come from KasaMonitor labels (protocol: legacy, klap, aes). Every column is aggregated by alias, so a plug keeps one row when its labels change (e.g. after an upgrade that adds labels); model / protocol come from a separate query joined on alias.",
      "id": 8,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
